# Business documentation

Business docs live in `docs/business/en.md` and `docs/business/fa.md`. They describe what Sino Persia is and what it does for customers, agents, admins, and sellers. They are not the technical spec.

When a change alters a user-facing feature, role, journey, status, commercial rule, or a stated limitation, update both files in the same change:

- Keep the same facts in both languages. Wording may differ; meaning may not.
- Update the "Last updated" date in both files.
- Describe the behavior a person can use, not file names, APIs, or schema.
- If a capability is unfinished or placeholder, say so. Do not document it as live.
- Skip the docs only for internal refactors that do not change what the product does.

```md
<!-- ❌ BAD: shop checkout now charges a card, but only en.md mentions it -->
<!-- ✅ GOOD: both en.md and fa.md say the shop submits a purchase request and payment still happens after a quote -->
```
